    "problem_statement": "Parser returns incorrect line numbers and truncated strings\n\nDescription\n\nWhen parsing .env files, the parser is returning incorrect line numbers and truncated strings in the Original objects. Line numbers appear to be off by 1 (showing line 2 instead of line 1) and strings are missing their last character.\n\nSteps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport io\nfrom dotenv.parser import parse_stream\n\n# Simple single line case\nresult = list(parse_stream(io.StringIO('a=b')))\nprint(f\"Expected: line=1, string='a=b'\")\nprint(f\"Actual: line={result[0].original.line}, string='{result[0].original.string}'\")\n\n# Multi-line case  \nresult = list(parse_stream(io.StringIO('a=b\\nc=d')))\nprint(f\"Expected first line: line=1, string='a=b\\\\n'\")\nprint(f\"Actual first line: line={result[0].original.line}, string='{result[0].original.string}'\")\nprint(f\"Expected second line: line=2, string='c=d'\") \nprint(f\"Actual second line: line={result[1].original.line}, string='{result[1].original.string}'\")\n```\n\nExpected output:\n```\nExpected: line=1, string='a=b'\nActual: line=1, string='a=b'\nExpected first line: line=1, string='a=b\\n'\nActual first line: line=1, string='a=b\\n'\nExpected second line: line=2, string='c=d'\nActual second line: line=2, string='c=d'\n```\n\nActual output:\n```\nExpected: line=1, string='a=b'\nActual: line=2, string='a='\nExpected first line: line=1, string='a=b\\n'\nActual first line: line=2, string='a=b'\nExpected second line: line=2, string='c=d'\nActual second line: line=3, string='c='\n```"
